PulseAudio
==========

url    = https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/pulseaudio/pulseaudio.git
tag    = v17.0
commit = 1f020889c9aa44ea0f63d7222e8c2b62c3f45f68
date   = 2024-01-12

tools/desktop/build-pipewire.sh builds the client side of this revision
(GitLab's archive of the tag, identical to the submodule, checked by
SHA-256) with tools/desktop/patches/pulseaudio-dragonfly.txt: libpulse,
libpulse-simple and the utilities (pactl, paplay, parec), installed in
/System/Library/PipeWire.  The PulseAudio daemon is not built: PipeWire's
pipewire-pulse serves PulseAudio applications (docs/desktop-pipewire.md).
Keep build output outside the submodule; when upgrading, update the tag
and checksum in build-pipewire.sh too.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later except as LICENSE notes (see LICENSE, LGPL,
GPL and individual file notices).  The client is built without D-Bus and
without the optional GPL dependencies LICENSE lists, which apply to the
server side, not built here.
Complete the file-level and asset provenance review and preserve
applicable notices and source obligations before distribution.

When upgrading, review dependencies, API and ABI compatibility, FoxynBSD
portability (the patch), license notices and the full desktop build and
runtime tests, including the audio check.
